@startuml activity-take-down-and-edit
' Spec 004 — taking down a published listing, and Admin edits (REQ-004-7, -8)
title Take down and edit (REQ-004-7/8)

start
:Admin opens a listing's Admin view;
if (Action?) then (take down)
  :Admin writes why and is told
  it cannot be undone;
  if (Still Published?) then (no)
    :Refuse — "This listing is
    no longer published." Nothing changes;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  if (Reason is 10–500 characters?) then (no)
    :Validation error — stays Published;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  :Status → Taken down, reason saved.
  The employer sees "Taken down" and the reason;
  :Record the time and the Admin;
  :No longer public (005);
  :Frees one open-listing slot (003);
  :Email the employer the reason (REQ-004-9);
  note right
    Final. Nobody can restore it.
    The employer posts a new listing.
    The listing is kept, never deleted.
  end note
  :Stay on the listing's Admin view, now
  Taken down, with a confirmation;
  stop
else (edit)
  if (Pending approval or Published?) then (no)
    :Refuse — "This listing can no longer be
    edited." No form is shown;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  :Admin changes any listing field, or this
  listing's business name or "about";
  note right
    Regions offered: the active ones,
    plus the one the listing is already in.
    Status, owner and submission time
    cannot be changed.
    The form says "The employer will be
    told what you changed."
  end note
  if (Still Pending approval or Published\nat the moment of saving?) then (no)
    :Refuse — say the listing can no
    longer be edited. Nothing saved;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  if (Still complete and valid?\n(REQ-003-4, business name REQ-003-2)) then (no)
    :Validation error — nothing saved;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  if (Anything actually changed?) then (no)
    :Nothing saved, no email. Back on the Admin
    view with "Nothing was changed.";
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  :Save. Status and place in the queue stay the same.
  No second approval is needed;
  :The account's business details are untouched;
  :Email the employer which parts changed (REQ-004-9);
  :Back on the listing's Admin view
  with a confirmation;
  note right
    Two Admins saving at the same time:
    the later save replaces the earlier one.
  end note
  stop
endif
@enduml
